<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<script src="./support.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
<x-dc>
<!-- @template name="Brand Deck" description="Whizlabs design-system presentation on deck-stage — logo, colour, type, components and UI kits." -->
<helmet>
<script src="./ds-base.js"></script>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Poppins:wght@300;400;500;600;700&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap">
<script src="https://unpkg.com/lucide@0.462.0/dist/umd/lucide.js"></script>
<style>body{margin:0;background:#26241f}</style>
</helmet>
<x-import component-from-global-scope="deck-stage" from="./deck-stage.js" width="1920" height="1080" hint-size="100%,100%">

<section data-label="Title" data-screen-label="01" data-speaker-notes="Before we look at a single screen, the reason this exists. Whizlabs ships a lot of surfaces — a marketing site, a learner app, practice tests, labs — and right now every one of them is a fresh set of decisions. Someone picks an orange, someone picks a spacing, someone picks a shadow. None of it is wrong on its own, but together it stops looking like one company. This deck is the fix: one place where those decisions are already made, so nobody has to make them again." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:space-between;padding:100px 100px 80px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b 0%,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20 100%);font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#fff;position:relative;overflow:hidden">
<span style="position:absolute;inset:0;background:radial-gradient(120% 120% at 100% 0%,rgba(255,255,255,.22),transparent 58%);pointer-events:none"></span>
<img src="../../assets/logo-lockup-mono.svg" alt="Whizlabs" style="position:relative;height:64px;width:auto;display:block;align-self:flex-start">
<div style="position:relative;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:32px">
<h1 style="margin:0;font-size:112px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.05;letter-spacing:-.025em">Design System</h1>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:38px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.4;color:rgba(255,255,255,.92);max-width:30ch">Foundations, components and UI kits for the Whizlabs certification-training platform.</p>
</div>
<p style="position:relative;margin:0;font-size:28px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:rgba(255,255,255,.75)">Version 1 · August 2026</p>
</section>

<section data-label="Contents" data-screen-label="02" data-speaker-notes="Quick map of where we're going. Foundations first — logo, colour, type, space — because those are the pieces everything else is built from. Then motion and states, then the components, then two full product surfaces built out of them. And I'll finish honestly, on what's still open. Roughly twenty minutes, and stop me wherever." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:100px 100px 80px;background:#fff;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#1a1917">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 64px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Contents</h2>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:36px 80px">
<div style="display:flex;gap:28px;align-items:baseline;border-top:2px solid #efece7;padding-top:24px"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:#f0602a">01</span><span style="font-size:36px;font-weight:500">The logo</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:28px;align-items:baseline;border-top:2px solid #efece7;padding-top:24px"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:#f0602a">05</span><span style="font-size:36px;font-weight:500">Motion and states</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:28px;align-items:baseline;border-top:2px solid #efece7;padding-top:24px"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:#f0602a">02</span><span style="font-size:36px;font-weight:500">Colour</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:28px;align-items:baseline;border-top:2px solid #efece7;padding-top:24px"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:#f0602a">06</span><span style="font-size:36px;font-weight:500">49 components, in detail</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:28px;align-items:baseline;border-top:2px solid #efece7;padding-top:24px"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:#f0602a">03</span><span style="font-size:36px;font-weight:500">Typography</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:28px;align-items:baseline;border-top:2px solid #efece7;padding-top:24px"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:#f0602a">07</span><span style="font-size:36px;font-weight:500">UI kits</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:28px;align-items:baseline;border-top:2px solid #efece7;padding-top:24px"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:#f0602a">04</span><span style="font-size:36px;font-weight:500">Space, radius, elevation</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:28px;align-items:baseline;border-top:2px solid #efece7;padding-top:24px"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:#f0602a">08</span><span style="font-size:36px;font-weight:500">Open items</span></div>
</div>
</section>

<section data-label="Logo" data-screen-label="03" data-speaker-notes="Start with the logo, because it's the thing that gets misused most. Three variants, and the reason there are exactly three is that people were previously improvising — stretching the lockup, dropping it on a dark background where the wordmark disappeared, or re-typing WHIZLABS in whatever font was to hand. Now there's a correct answer for every context. And critically, size sets the height, not the width — that one rule prevents most of the distortion I used to see." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:100px 100px 80px;background:#fff;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#1a1917">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">The logo</h2>
<p style="margin:0 0 56px;font-size:34px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43;max-width:52ch">Three vector variants. <span style="font-weight:500">Size sets the height</span> — width follows the artwork.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr;gap:28px;flex:1">
<div style="border:2px solid #efece7;border-radius:20px;display:grid;place-items:center;padding:40px"><img src="../../assets/logo-lockup.svg" alt="Whizlabs" style="height:76px;width:auto"></div>
<div style="border:2px solid #efece7;border-radius:20px;display:grid;place-items:center;padding:40px"><img src="../../assets/logo-mark.svg" alt="Whizlabs mark" style="height:104px;width:auto"></div>
<div style="background:#1a1917;border-radius:20px;display:grid;place-items:center;padding:40px"><img src="../../assets/logo-lockup-inverse.svg" alt="Whizlabs" style="height:76px;width:auto"></div>
<div style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fff3ee,#fff8ea);border:2px solid #ffe7dc;border-radius:20px;display:grid;place-items:center;padding:40px"><img src="../../assets/logo-lockup.svg" alt="Whizlabs" style="height:52px;width:auto"></div>
</div>
<p style="margin:44px 0 0;font-size:28px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.5;color:#6a655c">Clear space equals the mark height. Minimum lockup height 16px. Never re-typeset the wordmark, recolour the gradient, or add effects.</p>
</section>

<section data-label="Gradient" data-screen-label="04" data-speaker-notes="Here's the decision that saved the most time. Rather than invent a palette and hope it matched the logo, I pulled the three gradient stops straight out of the vector and built everything outward from them. So when you ask why the primary button is this particular orange — it isn't a taste call anybody has to defend. It's the middle of your own logo. That means nobody has to argue about brand colour again, and nothing drifts." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:space-between;padding:100px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20);font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#fff">
<h2 style="margin:0;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em;max-width:24ch">The gradient is the palette</h2>
<div style="display:flex;gap:80px;align-items:flex-end">
<div><p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:32px;font-weight:600">#e8402b</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:28px;font-weight:300;opacity:.85">Red · 0%</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:32px;font-weight:600">#f0602a</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:28px;font-weight:300;opacity:.85">Vermilion · 52%</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:32px;font-weight:600">#f78b20</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:28px;font-weight:300;opacity:.85">Orange · 100%</p></div>
</div>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:34px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;max-width:60ch">Every tint and shade in the system is built outward from these three stops, lifted straight from the logo vector. Allowed on primary buttons, 4px accent rules, thumbnail bands and progress fills — never as a page background.</p>
</section>

<section data-label="Ramps" data-screen-label="05" data-speaker-notes="The ramps are what make that usable in practice. One brand orange isn't enough to build an interface — you need a hover state, a selected row, a disabled state, a tint behind a warning. Without a defined ramp, people eyeball those, and eyeballed tints are where inconsistency creeps in fastest. The neutral is worth a word too: it's deliberately warm with no blue in it, because a cool grey next to this orange makes both look slightly wrong." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:100px 100px 80px;background:#fff;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#1a1917">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 56px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Colour ramps</h2>
<p style="margin:0 0 20px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Orange — primary</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;margin-bottom:44px">
<div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#fff5f0"></div><div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#ffe7dc"></div><div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#ffcab2"></div><div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#fca781"></div><div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#f78454"></div><div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#f0602a"></div><div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#d94b1c"></div><div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#b23b17"></div><div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#8c2f14"></div><div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#6b2511"></div>
</div>
<p style="margin:0 0 20px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Ink — warm neutral</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;margin-bottom:44px">
<div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#f9f7f4"></div><div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#efece7"></div><div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#e2ded7"></div><div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#cbc6bd"></div><div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#aca69c"></div><div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#8a847a"></div><div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#6a655c"></div><div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#4e4a43"></div><div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#37342e"></div><div style="flex:1;height:96px;border-radius:10px;background:#1a1917"></div>
</div>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:34px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43;max-width:64ch">The neutral carries a trace of the brand's warmth and no blue at all, so nothing on the page competes with the orange or fights the near-black wordmark.</p>
</section>

<section data-label="Typography" data-screen-label="06" data-speaker-notes="Poppins is your typeface, so it's the system's typeface — no substitution, no negotiation. What's needed here isn't the font choice, it's the settings. Left alone, Poppins gets used at whatever weight and tracking each person likes, and the result reads as several different brands. Fixing the weights, the tracking and the line-height means a heading built by someone who's never seen this deck still comes out looking like Whizlabs." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:100px 100px 80px;background:#f9f7f4;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#1a1917">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Poppins</h2>
<p style="margin:0 0 60px;font-size:34px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43;max-width:56ch">One family for structure and reading text, with IBM Plex Mono for exam machinery.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:72px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em;line-height:1.1">Get certified. Faster.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 40px;font-size:44px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#37342e">Section heading, 600</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 48px;font-size:34px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.7;color:#4e4a43;max-width:52ch">Every practice test is written against the current exam blueprint, and every question carries a written explanation.</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:56px;align-items:baseline;border-top:2px solid #e2ded7;padding-top:36px">
<span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:52px;font-weight:600">42:17</span>
<span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:36px;font-weight:500;color:#6a655c">SAA-C03</span>
<span style="font-size:28px;font-weight:400;color:#6a655c;max-width:34ch;line-height:1.5">Mono is reserved for codes, timers, scores and question numbers.</span>
</div>
</section>

<section data-label="Type rules" data-screen-label="07" data-speaker-notes="These three rules are the ones people push back on, so let me justify them. Poppins is geometric and wide, which means the habits borrowed from other typefaces actively hurt it — 800 goes clumsy at headline sizes, tight tracking closes the counters, and standard web line-height makes paragraphs feel cramped because there's more ink on every line. Encoding that as three rules means nobody has to learn it the slow way." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:100px 100px 80px;background:#fff;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#1a1917">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Three rules Poppins forces</h2>
<p style="margin:0 0 64px;font-size:34px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43;max-width:56ch">It is geometric, wide and near-monolinear, and the system encodes the consequences.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:40px;flex:1">
<div style="background:#f9f7f4;border-radius:20px;padding:48px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px">
<span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:#f0602a">01</span>
<span style="font-size:40px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;line-height:1.2">Weights stop at 700</span>
<span style="font-size:28px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.6;color:#4e4a43">800 is clumsy at headline sizes. Display and H1 are 700, H2 and H3 are 600, labels 500.</span>
</div>
<div style="background:#f9f7f4;border-radius:20px;padding:48px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px">
<span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:#f0602a">02</span>
<span style="font-size:40px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;line-height:1.2">Tracking stays light</span>
<span style="font-size:28px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.6;color:#4e4a43">Minus .01em normally, minus .02em at display sizes. Tighter would close the counters.</span>
</div>
<div style="background:#f9f7f4;border-radius:20px;padding:48px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px">
<span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:#f0602a">03</span>
<span style="font-size:40px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;line-height:1.2">Lines breathe more</span>
<span style="font-size:28px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.6;color:#4e4a43">Body is 16 on 1.7 and paragraphs cap near 58 characters, not 68.</span>
</div>
</div>
<p style="margin:44px 0 0;font-size:28px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.5;color:#6a655c">Poppins Light 300 is loaded but reserved — it is the weight the logotype resembles, so keeping it out of the interface preserves the distinction.</p>
</section>

<section data-label="Space" data-screen-label="08" data-speaker-notes="Space, radius and elevation are the least glamorous slide here and probably the highest-value one. This is where inconsistency is most visible and least defensible — a card with a fourteen-pixel corner next to one with eight, padding that's sixteen here and twenty there. Nobody notices any single instance. Everybody notices the accumulation. Fixing it to one scale means a screen assembled by two different people still lines up." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:100px 100px 80px;background:#fff;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#1a1917">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 56px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Space, radius, elevation</h2>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:64px 80px;flex:1">
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 28px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Spacing — 4px base</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-end">
<div style="width:24px;height:24px;border-radius:4px;background:#ffcab2"></div><div style="width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:4px;background:#fca781"></div><div style="width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:4px;background:#f78454"></div><div style="width:60px;height:60px;border-radius:5px;background:#f0602a"></div><div style="width:80px;height:80px;border-radius:6px;background:#d94b1c"></div><div style="width:104px;height:104px;border-radius:7px;background:#b23b17"></div>
</div>
<p style="margin:28px 0 0;font-size:28px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43">16 or 24 inside cards, 32 and 48 between blocks, 96 between page sections.</p>
</div>
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 28px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Radii</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:20px;align-items:flex-end">
<div style="width:88px;height:72px;background:#f9f7f4;border:2px solid #e2ded7;border-radius:4px"></div><div style="width:88px;height:72px;background:#f9f7f4;border:2px solid #e2ded7;border-radius:6px"></div><div style="width:88px;height:72px;background:#f9f7f4;border:2px solid #e2ded7;border-radius:10px"></div><div style="width:88px;height:72px;background:#f9f7f4;border:2px solid #e2ded7;border-radius:14px"></div><div style="width:88px;height:72px;background:#f9f7f4;border:2px solid #e2ded7;border-radius:20px"></div><div style="width:112px;height:56px;background:#f9f7f4;border:2px solid #e2ded7;border-radius:999px"></div>
</div>
<p style="margin:28px 0 0;font-size:28px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43">14px is the card workhorse. The pill is for badges, search and progress only.</p>
</div>
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 28px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Elevation</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:24px">
<div style="flex:1;height:88px;background:#fff;border-radius:14px;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(26,25,23,.08),0 1px 2px rgba(26,25,23,.04)"></div><div style="flex:1;height:88px;background:#fff;border-radius:14px;box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(26,25,23,.08)"></div><div style="flex:1;height:88px;background:#fff;border-radius:14px;box-shadow:0 12px 28px rgba(26,25,23,.10)"></div><div style="flex:1;height:88px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20);border-radius:14px;box-shadow:0 8px 20px rgba(240,96,42,.28)"></div>
</div>
<p style="margin:28px 0 0;font-size:28px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43">Five neutral steps on the ink value, never black, plus one brand glow.</p>
</div>
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 28px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">The card recipe</p>
<div style="background:#fff;border:2px solid #efece7;border-radius:14px;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(26,25,23,.08);padding:32px;position:relative;overflow:hidden">
<span style="position:absolute;inset:0 0 auto 0;height:6px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20)"></span>
<p style="margin:8px 0 8px;font-size:32px;font-weight:600">White, hairline, 14px, shadow-sm</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:28px;font-weight:400;color:#6a655c">The only accent is a 4px gradient rule on the top edge. No coloured left borders.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section data-label="Motion" data-screen-label="09" data-speaker-notes="Interaction states matter more than they look like they should, because they're what makes an interface feel finished. Hover, press, focus, selection — one behaviour each, applied everywhere. And focus is the accessibility one I'd ask you not to trade away: it's the only way a keyboard user knows where they are. Note also what's absent. No bounce, no spring, no scroll animation. On a platform where people sit timed exams, motion that draws attention to itself is a cost, not a feature." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:100px 100px 80px;background:#1a1917;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#fff">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Motion and states</h2>
<p style="margin:0 0 64px;font-size:34px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;color:#cbc6bd;max-width:56ch">One curve, five durations. Motion confirms an action; it never decorates.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:40px 80px;flex:1">
<div style="border-top:2px solid #4e4a43;padding-top:28px"><p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:36px;font-weight:600">Hover</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:28px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.6;color:#aca69c">Cards lift 2px and deepen their shadow. Primary buttons flatten to solid orange-600 and gain the brand glow.</p></div>
<div style="border-top:2px solid #4e4a43;padding-top:28px"><p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:36px;font-weight:600">Press</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:28px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.6;color:#aca69c">Scale .97 with no colour change, 80ms. Identical on every clickable control.</p></div>
<div style="border-top:2px solid #4e4a43;padding-top:28px"><p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:36px;font-weight:600">Focus</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:28px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.6;color:#aca69c">A 3px orange ring on fields, a 3px orange outline everywhere else. One global rule, never removed.</p></div>
<div style="border-top:2px solid #4e4a43;padding-top:28px"><p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:36px;font-weight:600">Selection</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:28px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.6;color:#aca69c">Orange-50 fill, orange-300 border, orange-700 text. The single selection idiom system-wide.</p></div>
</div>
<p style="margin:48px 0 0;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:32px;font-weight:500;color:#f78b20">80 · 140 · 200 · 320 · 520ms — cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.3,1)</p>
</section>

<section data-label="Inventory" data-screen-label="10" data-speaker-notes="Twenty-six components, and the point of the inventory is coverage. If something a designer needs isn't in here, they'll build it themselves, and that's the moment the system starts leaking. So this set is sized to actually build your screens — not a showcase, a working kit. Each one carries a props contract and a usage note, so an engineer can pick it up without asking a designer what it's for." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:100px 100px 80px;background:#fff;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#1a1917">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Component inventory</h2>
<p style="margin:0 0 48px;font-size:34px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43;max-width:58ch">Forty-nine components in eight groups. Each ships with a props contract, a usage note and a live specimen card.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:36px 32px;flex:1;align-content:start">
<div style="border-top:4px solid #f0602a;padding-top:28px"><p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:30px;font-weight:600">Brand</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:24px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.55;color:#4e4a43">Logo · Icon</p></div>
<div style="border-top:4px solid #f0602a;padding-top:28px"><p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:30px;font-weight:600">Core</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:24px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.55;color:#4e4a43">Button · IconButton · Badge · Tag · Card · Avatar</p></div>
<div style="border-top:4px solid #f0602a;padding-top:28px"><p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:30px;font-weight:600">Forms</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:24px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.55;color:#4e4a43">Input · Select · Checkbox · Radio · Switch · SearchField · Slider · NumberField · Rating · ToggleButton · ButtonGroup · Fab · Autocomplete · TransferList</p></div>
<div style="border-top:4px solid #f0602a;padding-top:28px"><p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:30px;font-weight:600">Feedback</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:24px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.55;color:#4e4a43">Alert · ProgressBar · ScoreRing · Skeleton · Dialog · Snackbar · Spinner · Backdrop</p></div>
<div style="border-top:4px solid #f0602a;padding-top:28px"><p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:30px;font-weight:600">Navigation</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:24px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.55;color:#4e4a43">Tabs · Breadcrumb · Pagination · SidebarNav · Stepper · Menu · BottomNav · Link</p></div>
<div style="border-top:4px solid #f0602a;padding-top:28px"><p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:30px;font-weight:600">Learning</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:24px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.55;color:#4e4a43">CourseCard · StatTile · LessonRow · QuestionCard</p></div>
<div style="border-top:4px solid #f0602a;padding-top:28px"><p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:30px;font-weight:600">Data display</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:24px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.55;color:#4e4a43">Divider · List · Table · Tooltip</p></div>
<div style="border-top:4px solid #f0602a;padding-top:28px"><p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:30px;font-weight:600">Surfaces</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:24px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.55;color:#4e4a43">Paper · Accordion · AppBar</p></div>
</div>
</section>

<section data-label="Controls" data-screen-label="11" data-speaker-notes="Worth seeing the components as real objects rather than a list. This is the payoff of everything before it — the button is the logo gradient, the badge tones are the status colours, the selected answer uses the one selection idiom, the progress fill is the same ramp. None of that was decided on this slide. It all came for free from the foundations, which is exactly the test of whether a system is working." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:100px 100px 80px;background:#f9f7f4;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#1a1917">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 56px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Controls in the flesh</h2>
<div style="display:flex;gap:28px;align-items:center;margin-bottom:48px;flex-wrap:wrap">
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;height:76px;padding:0 44px;border-radius:14px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20);color:#fff;font-size:32px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em">Start free trial</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;height:76px;padding:0 44px;border-radius:14px;background:#fff;border:2px solid #e2ded7;color:#26241f;font-size:32px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em">View syllabus</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;height:76px;padding:0 44px;border-radius:14px;border:2px solid #f0602a;color:#d94b1c;font-size:32px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em">Outline</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;height:76px;padding:0 44px;border-radius:14px;color:#4e4a43;font-size:32px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em">Ghost</span>
</div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:20px;align-items:center;margin-bottom:56px;flex-wrap:wrap">
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:12px 26px;border-radius:999px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20);color:#fff;font-size:26px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase">Bestseller</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:12px 26px;border-radius:999px;background:#efece7;color:#4e4a43;font-size:26px;font-weight:600">Associate</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:12px 26px;border-radius:999px;background:#d8f3e3;color:#0b7a3c;font-size:26px;font-weight:600">Passed</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:12px 26px;border-radius:999px;background:#fdf0d5;color:#8a5a06;font-size:26px;font-weight:600">Expiring</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:12px 26px;border-radius:999px;background:#fef2f0;color:#a4271a;font-size:26px;font-weight:600">Failed</span>
</div>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:40px;flex:1">
<div style="background:#fff;border:2px solid #efece7;border-radius:14px;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(26,25,23,.08);padding:36px">
<p style="margin:0 0 20px;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:26px;font-weight:600;color:#6a655c">Q12 / 65</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 28px;font-size:30px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.55">An application must decouple order intake from fulfilment and guarantee exactly-once processing.</p>
<div style="padding:22px 26px;border-radius:10px;border:2px solid #fca781;background:#fff5f0;font-size:28px;font-weight:500;color:#37342e">Amazon SQS FIFO queue</div>
</div>
<div style="background:#fff;border:2px solid #efece7;border-radius:14px;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(26,25,23,.08);padding:36px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;gap:28px">
<p style="margin:0;font-size:30px;font-weight:500">Course progress</p>
<div style="height:20px;border-radius:999px;background:#efece7;overflow:hidden"><div style="width:62%;height:100%;border-radius:999px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20)"></div></div>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:56px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">82%</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:28px;font-weight:400;color:#6a655c">Average mock score</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section data-label="Buttons" data-screen-label="12" data-speaker-notes="Buttons carry more weight than any other component, so they get the most definition. Six variants, four sizes, and a rule I'd hold to: one primary per view. The moment a screen has two gradient buttons, neither reads as the main action. Notice the primary is the logo gradient and hover flattens it to solid — that's not decoration, it's how you tell pressed-and-loading apart from idle at a glance." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:100px 100px 80px;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#1a1917;background:#fff">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Buttons</h2>
<p style="margin:0 0 56px;font-size:34px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43;max-width:58ch">Six variants, four sizes. One primary per view — a second gradient button means neither reads as the main action.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Variants</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:52px">
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;height:72px;padding:0 40px;border-radius:14px;font-size:30px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20);color:#fff;box-shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(26,25,23,.06)">Start free trial</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;height:72px;padding:0 40px;border-radius:14px;font-size:30px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;background:#fff;border:2px solid #e2ded7;color:#26241f">View syllabus</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;height:72px;padding:0 40px;border-radius:14px;font-size:30px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;border:2px solid #f0602a;color:#d94b1c">Outline</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;height:72px;padding:0 40px;border-radius:14px;font-size:30px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#4e4a43">Ghost</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;height:72px;padding:0 40px;border-radius:14px;font-size:30px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;border:2px solid rgba(255,255,255,.5);color:#fff;background:#37342e">Inverse</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;height:72px;padding:0 40px;border-radius:14px;font-size:30px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;background:#e8402b;color:#fff">Delete</span>
</div>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.15fr 1fr;gap:72px;flex:1">
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Sizes — 32 / 40 / 48 / 56</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:20px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap">
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;height:48px;padding:0 26px;border-radius:6px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20);color:#fff;font-size:24px;font-weight:600">Small</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;height:60px;padding:0 34px;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20);color:#fff;font-size:28px;font-weight:600">Medium</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;height:72px;padding:0 40px;border-radius:14px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20);color:#fff;font-size:30px;font-weight:600">Large</span>
</div>
</div>
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">States</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap">
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;height:72px;padding:0 40px;border-radius:14px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;background:#d94b1c;color:#fff;box-shadow:0 8px 20px rgba(240,96,42,.28)">Hover</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;height:72px;padding:0 40px;border-radius:14px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20);color:#fff;transform:scale(.97)">Press</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;height:72px;padding:0 40px;border-radius:14px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20);color:#fff;opacity:.45">Disabled</span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p style="margin:24px 0 0;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:25px;font-weight:500;color:#8a847a;border-top:2px solid #e2ded7;padding-top:20px">variant · size · fullWidth · leadingIcon · trailingIcon · disabled · as</p>
</section>

<section data-label="Badges and tags" data-screen-label="13" data-speaker-notes="Two components people constantly confuse, so the distinction is worth stating out loud. A badge is read-only — it tells you something's state. A tag is interactive — you click it to filter. Same rough shape, completely different contract, and mixing them teaches users that some pills do nothing when clicked. That's why the badge is a pill and the tag is a rectangle: the shape itself signals which one you're looking at." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:100px 100px 80px;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#1a1917;background:#f9f7f4">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Badges and tags</h2>
<p style="margin:0 0 56px;font-size:34px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43;max-width:58ch">A badge reports state and is read-only. A tag is a filter you click. Different shapes so the difference is visible before you try.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Badge — tinted</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:44px">
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:12px 26px;border-radius:999px;background:#fff5f0;color:#b23b17;font-size:26px;font-weight:600;border:2px solid #ffcab2">Associate</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:12px 26px;border-radius:999px;background:#efece7;color:#4e4a43;font-size:26px;font-weight:600;border:2px solid #e2ded7">780 questions</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:12px 26px;border-radius:999px;background:#d8f3e3;color:#0b7a3c;font-size:26px;font-weight:600;border:2px solid #b6e5cb">Passed</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:12px 26px;border-radius:999px;background:#fdf0d5;color:#8a5a06;font-size:26px;font-weight:600;border:2px solid #f6ddab">Expiring</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:12px 26px;border-radius:999px;background:#fef2f0;color:#a4271a;font-size:26px;font-weight:600;border:2px solid #fbbcb2">Failed</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:12px 26px;border-radius:999px;background:#dbeafe;color:#1d4ed8;font-size:26px;font-weight:600;border:2px solid #bcd4fd">Updated</span>
</div>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Badge — solid</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:44px">
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:12px 26px;border-radius:999px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20);color:#fff;font-size:26px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase">Bestseller</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:12px 26px;border-radius:999px;background:#1a1917;color:#fff;font-size:26px;font-weight:600;">New</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:12px 26px;border-radius:999px;background:#0b7a3c;color:#fff;font-size:26px;font-weight:600;">Complete</span>
</div>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Tag — filter chip</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;flex:1;align-content:flex-start">
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;height:60px;padding:0 26px;border-radius:6px;background:#fff5f0;border:2px solid #fca781;color:#b23b17;font-size:28px;font-weight:500">AWS</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;height:60px;padding:0 26px;border-radius:6px;background:#fff;border:2px solid #e2ded7;color:#4e4a43;font-size:28px;font-weight:500">Microsoft Azure</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;height:60px;padding:0 26px;border-radius:6px;background:#fff;border:2px solid #e2ded7;color:#4e4a43;font-size:28px;font-weight:500">Kubernetes</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;height:60px;padding:0 26px;border-radius:6px;background:#fff;border:2px solid #e2ded7;color:#4e4a43;font-size:28px;font-weight:500">Terraform<span style="color:#8a847a">&times;</span></span>
</div>
<p style="margin:24px 0 0;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:25px;font-weight:500;color:#8a847a;border-top:2px solid #e2ded7;padding-top:20px">Badge — tone · solid · uppercase &nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp; Tag — active · onRemove</p>
</section>

<section data-label="Cards and avatars" data-screen-label="14" data-speaker-notes="One card recipe, and I mean one. White, hairline border, fourteen-pixel corner, small shadow. The only permitted decoration is that four-pixel gradient rule across the top. I'm being deliberately strict because cards are where systems fall apart fastest — everyone wants their own variant, and six card styles on a page is what makes a product look assembled by committee. Hover lifts two pixels, which is enough to say clickable without anything jumping." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:100px 100px 80px;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#1a1917;background:#f9f7f4">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Cards and avatars</h2>
<p style="margin:0 0 56px;font-size:34px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43;max-width:58ch">One recipe, three states. The only permitted accent is a 4px gradient rule on the top edge — never a coloured left border.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:36px;margin-bottom:56px">
<div style="background:#fff;border:2px solid #efece7;border-radius:14px;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(26,25,23,.08);padding:36px">
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:32px;font-weight:600">Resting</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:26px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.5;color:#6a655c">Hairline ink-100, radius 14, shadow-sm.</p>
</div>
<div style="background:#fff;border:2px solid #e2ded7;border-radius:14px;box-shadow:0 12px 28px rgba(26,25,23,.10);padding:36px;transform:translateY(-6px)">
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:32px;font-weight:600">Hover</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:26px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.5;color:#6a655c">Lifts 2px, shadow deepens to lg.</p>
</div>
<div style="background:#fff;border:2px solid #efece7;border-radius:14px;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(26,25,23,.08);padding:36px;position:relative;overflow:hidden">
<span style="position:absolute;inset:0 0 auto 0;height:8px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20)"></span>
<p style="margin:8px 0 12px;font-size:32px;font-weight:600">Accented</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:26px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.5;color:#6a655c">Gradient rule, top edge only.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Avatar — gradient initials when no image</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:28px;align-items:center;flex:1">
<span style="width:96px;height:96px;border-radius:999px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20);color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:36px;font-weight:700">PN</span>
<span style="width:76px;height:76px;border-radius:999px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20);color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:28px;font-weight:700">DO</span>
<span style="width:60px;height:60px;border-radius:999px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20);color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:24px;font-weight:700">SO</span>
<span style="display:flex;margin-left:20px">
<span style="width:64px;height:64px;border-radius:999px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20);color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:24px;font-weight:700;box-shadow:0 0 0 5px #f9f7f4">AB</span>
<span style="width:64px;height:64px;border-radius:999px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20);color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:24px;font-weight:700;box-shadow:0 0 0 5px #f9f7f4;margin-left:-18px">CD</span>
<span style="width:64px;height:64px;border-radius:999px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20);color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:24px;font-weight:700;box-shadow:0 0 0 5px #f9f7f4;margin-left:-18px">EF</span>
</span>
</div>
<p style="margin:24px 0 0;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:25px;font-weight:500;color:#8a847a;border-top:2px solid #e2ded7;padding-top:20px">Card — interactive · padding · accent &nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp; Avatar — name · src · size</p>
</section>

<section data-label="Text inputs" data-screen-label="15" data-speaker-notes="Fields are where accessibility either happens or doesn't. Every one of these has a visible label, room for a hint, and a distinct error state — because a red border alone doesn't tell a screen reader anything, and a placeholder that vanishes when you type isn't a label. The focus ring is the orange at twenty-eight percent, and I'd ask you never to remove it. The pill-shaped search is the one intentional exception to the ten-pixel radius, because search reads as a different kind of object." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:76px 100px 56px;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#1a1917;background:#fff">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Text inputs</h2>
<p style="margin:0 0 56px;font-size:34px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43;max-width:58ch">Every field carries a real label, room for a hint, and a distinct error state. Focus is never removed.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:44px 56px;flex:1;align-content:start">
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:28px;font-weight:500">Work email</p>
<div style="height:76px;border:2px solid #e2ded7;border-radius:10px;background:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;padding:0 26px;font-size:28px;color:#8a847a">you@company.com</div>
<p style="margin:14px 0 0;font-size:26px;color:#6a655c">Used for your certificate.</p>
</div>
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:28px;font-weight:500">Full name</p>
<div style="height:76px;border:2px solid #f0602a;border-radius:10px;background:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;padding:0 26px;font-size:28px;color:#1a1917;box-shadow:0 0 0 6px rgba(240,96,42,.28)">Priya Nair</div>
<p style="margin:14px 0 0;font-size:26px;color:#6a655c">Focused — 3px ring, orange border.</p>
</div>
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:28px;font-weight:500">Password</p>
<div style="height:76px;border:2px solid #e8402b;border-radius:10px;background:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;padding:0 26px;font-size:28px;color:#1a1917">hunter22</div>
<p style="margin:14px 0 0;font-size:26px;color:#a4271a">Must be at least 12 characters.</p>
</div>
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:28px;font-weight:500">Sort by</p>
<div style="height:76px;border:2px solid #e2ded7;border-radius:10px;background:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:0 26px;font-size:28px;color:#1a1917">Most popular<span style="color:#8a847a;font-size:22px">&#9660;</span></div>
<p style="margin:14px 0 0;font-size:26px;color:#6a655c">Select — native, styled to match.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="margin-top:12px">
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Search — the one pill-shaped field</p>
<div style="height:88px;border:2px solid #e2ded7;border-radius:999px;background:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:22px;padding:0 36px;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(26,25,23,.08);max-width:840px">
<span style="color:#aca69c;font-size:34px">&#8981;</span><span style="font-size:28px;color:#8a847a">Search courses, certifications, labs</span>
</div>
</div>
<p style="margin:24px 0 0;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:25px;font-weight:500;color:#8a847a;border-top:2px solid #e2ded7;padding-top:20px">label · hint · error · leadingIcon · trailingIcon · size</p>
</section>

<section data-label="Selection controls" data-screen-label="16" data-speaker-notes="Checkbox, radio, switch — and the rule that decides between them. Checkbox for many-of-many, radio for one-of-many, switch only for something that applies the instant you flip it. A switch sitting above a Save button is a bug, not a style choice. The boxed radio on the right is the one I'd draw your attention to: it's the practice-test answer option, and it's a distinct treatment because tapping a small circle on a phone during a timed exam is genuinely hard." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:100px 100px 80px;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#1a1917;background:#f9f7f4">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Selection controls</h2>
<p style="margin:0 0 56px;font-size:34px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43;max-width:58ch">Checkbox for many, radio for one, switch only for settings that apply instantly. Checked states fill with the brand gradient.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.25fr;gap:72px;flex:1">
