</section>

<section data-label="Range and steppers" data-screen-label="20" data-speaker-notes="Three ways to enter a number, and the choice between them isn't arbitrary. A slider is for approximate values where feeling the range matters. A stepper is for exact small integers — seat counts, attempt limits. A rating is a scale with social meaning. Getting this wrong is how you end up with a slider for someone's team size, which nobody can set precisely, or a text field for a rating, which nobody fills in." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:100px 100px 80px;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#1a1917;background:#fff">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Range, steppers and rating</h2>
<p style="margin:0 0 52px;font-size:34px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43;max-width:58ch">A slider for approximate values, a stepper for exact small integers, a rating for a scale with social meaning.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr;gap:72px;flex:1;align-content:start">
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Slider</p>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:16px;font-size:28px"><span style="color:#6a655c">Questions per session</span><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-weight:600">40</span></div>
<div style="position:relative;height:24px;display:flex;align-items:center;margin-bottom:52px">
<div style="position:absolute;inset:auto 0;height:10px;border-radius:999px;background:#efece7"></div>
<div style="position:absolute;left:0;width:38%;height:10px;border-radius:999px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20)"></div>
<span style="position:absolute;left:38%;transform:translateX(-50%);width:36px;height:36px;border-radius:999px;background:#fff;border:4px solid #f0602a;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(26,25,23,.2)"></span>
</div>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Rating</p>
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:16px">
<span style="font-size:44px;letter-spacing:4px;color:#f9a825">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;<span style="color:#e2ded7">&#9733;</span></span>
<span style="font-size:34px;font-weight:700">4.6</span>
<span style="font-size:28px;color:#6a655c">(1,840)</span>
</div>
</div>
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Stepper</p>
<div style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;height:80px;border:2px solid #e2ded7;border-radius:10px;background:#fff;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(26,25,23,.06);margin-bottom:52px">
<span style="width:72px;height:100%;display:grid;place-items:center;border-right:2px solid #efece7;font-size:34px;color:#4e4a43">&minus;</span>
<span style="width:120px;text-align:center;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:32px;font-weight:600">12</span>
<span style="width:72px;height:100%;display:grid;place-items:center;border-left:2px solid #efece7;font-size:34px;color:#4e4a43">+</span>
</div>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Segmented toggle</p>
<div style="display:inline-flex">
<span style="padding:22px 32px;background:#fff5f0;color:#b23b17;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;border:3px solid #f78454;border-radius:10px 0 0 10px;position:relative;z-index:2;box-shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(26,25,23,.06)">Timed</span>
<span style="padding:22px 32px;background:#fff;color:#6a655c;font-size:28px;font-weight:500;border:3px solid #e2ded7;margin-left:-3px">Study mode</span>
<span style="padding:22px 32px;background:#fff;color:#6a655c;font-size:28px;font-weight:500;border:3px solid #e2ded7;border-radius:0 10px 10px 0;margin-left:-3px">Review</span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p style="margin:24px 0 0;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:25px;font-weight:500;color:#8a847a;border-top:2px solid #e2ded7;padding-top:20px">Slider &middot; NumberField &middot; Rating &middot; ToggleButton</p>
</section>

<section data-label="Search and pickers" data-screen-label="21" data-speaker-notes="Autocomplete is doing real work on a platform with five hundred exams — nobody browses to find SAA-C03, they type it. The meta column on the right carries the question count, so the choice is informed before the click. Transfer list is deliberately scoped to admin surfaces only: it's a good pattern for a manager assigning exams to a team, and a bad one for a learner mid-study." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:100px 100px 80px;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#1a1917;background:#f9f7f4">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Search and pickers</h2>
<p style="margin:0 0 52px;font-size:34px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43;max-width:58ch">With 500 exams in the catalogue, typing beats browsing. Suggestions carry a count so the choice is informed before the click.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.15fr;gap:64px;flex:1;align-content:start">
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Autocomplete</p>
<div style="height:80px;border:2px solid #f0602a;border-radius:10px;background:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:20px;padding:0 26px;box-shadow:0 0 0 6px rgba(240,96,42,.28)">
<span style="color:#aca69c;font-size:30px">&#8981;</span><span style="font-size:28px">solutions arch</span>
</div>
<div style="margin-top:12px;border:2px solid #e2ded7;border-radius:10px;background:#fff;box-shadow:0 12px 28px rgba(26,25,23,.1);overflow:hidden">
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:22px 26px;font-size:27px;background:#f9f7f4"><span style="font-weight:500">AWS Solutions Architect &ndash; Associate</span><span style="color:#8a847a">780 q</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:22px 26px;font-size:27px;border-top:2px solid #efece7"><span>Azure Solutions Architect Expert</span><span style="color:#8a847a">410 q</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:22px 26px;font-size:27px;border-top:2px solid #efece7"><span>GCP Professional Cloud Architect</span><span style="color:#8a847a">540 q</span></div>
</div>
</div>
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Transfer list — admin surfaces only</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:20px">
<div style="flex:1;border:2px solid #e2ded7;border-radius:10px;background:#fff;overflow:hidden">
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:18px 22px;background:#f9f7f4;border-bottom:2px solid #efece7;font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#4e4a43"><span>All exams</span><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;color:#8a847a">3</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:20px 22px;font-size:26px">Azure AZ-305<span style="color:#f0602a;font-weight:700">+</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:20px 22px;font-size:26px;border-top:2px solid #efece7">GCP Architect<span style="color:#f0602a;font-weight:700">+</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:20px 22px;font-size:26px;border-top:2px solid #efece7">CKA<span style="color:#f0602a;font-weight:700">+</span></div>
</div>
<div style="flex:1;border:2px solid #e2ded7;border-radius:10px;background:#fff;overflow:hidden">
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:18px 22px;background:#f9f7f4;border-bottom:2px solid #efece7;font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#4e4a43"><span>In this path</span><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;color:#8a847a">2</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:20px 22px;font-size:26px">AWS SAA-C03<span style="color:#f0602a;font-weight:700">&minus;</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:20px 22px;font-size:26px;border-top:2px solid #efece7">Terraform<span style="color:#f0602a;font-weight:700">&minus;</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p style="margin:24px 0 0;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:25px;font-weight:500;color:#8a847a;border-top:2px solid #e2ded7;padding-top:20px">Autocomplete &middot; TransferList &middot; SearchField</p>
</section>

<section data-label="Tables and lists" data-screen-label="22" data-speaker-notes="Tables are where the mono face earns its place. Scores, exam codes and durations all go mono so the digits align down the column — scan a list of results and your eye finds the outlier immediately. That's not a stylistic preference, it's the difference between a table you can read and one you have to parse. The uppercase header band and the hairline rows keep the structure visible without adding borders everywhere." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:76px 100px 56px;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#1a1917;background:#fff">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Tables and lists</h2>
<p style="margin:0 0 52px;font-size:34px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43;max-width:58ch">Codes, scores and durations go mono so digits align down the column. Uppercase header band, hairline rows, no vertical rules.</p>
<div style="border:2px solid #efece7;border-radius:14px;overflow:hidden;background:#fff;margin-bottom:40px;flex:0 0 auto">
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.2fr 1fr 1fr 1fr;background:#f9f7f4;border-bottom:2px solid #e2ded7;padding:18px 28px;font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">
<span>Exam</span><span>Code</span><span style="text-align:right">Score</span><span style="text-align:right">Result</span></div>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.2fr 1fr 1fr 1fr;padding:17px 28px;font-size:27px;align-items:center">
<span style="font-weight:500">Solutions Architect &ndash; Associate</span><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;color:#4e4a43">SAA-C03</span><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;text-align:right">792</span><span style="text-align:right"><span style="background:#d8f3e3;color:#0b7a3c;padding:8px 18px;border-radius:999px;font-size:24px;font-weight:600">Passed</span></span></div>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.2fr 1fr 1fr 1fr;padding:17px 28px;font-size:27px;align-items:center;border-top:2px solid #efece7">
<span style="font-weight:500">Developer &ndash; Associate</span><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;color:#4e4a43">DVA-C02</span><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;text-align:right">684</span><span style="text-align:right"><span style="background:#fef2f0;color:#a4271a;padding:8px 18px;border-radius:999px;font-size:24px;font-weight:600">Failed</span></span></div>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.2fr 1fr 1fr 1fr;padding:17px 28px;font-size:27px;align-items:center;border-top:2px solid #efece7">
<span style="font-weight:500">Terraform Associate</span><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;color:#4e4a43">TA-003</span><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;text-align:right">810</span><span style="text-align:right"><span style="background:#d8f3e3;color:#0b7a3c;padding:8px 18px;border-radius:999px;font-size:24px;font-weight:600">Passed</span></span></div>
</div>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.3fr 1fr;gap:44px;flex:0 0 auto;align-items:start">
<div style="border:2px solid #efece7;border-radius:14px;overflow:hidden;background:#fff">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:20px;padding:18px 28px"><span style="flex:1"><span style="display:block;font-size:28px;font-weight:600">Certificate of completion</span><span style="display:block;font-size:24px;color:#6a655c;margin-top:4px">PDF &middot; 240 KB</span></span><span style="font-size:24px;color:#6a655c">Download</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:20px;padding:18px 28px;border-top:2px solid #efece7;background:#f9f7f4"><span style="flex:1"><span style="display:block;font-size:28px;font-weight:600">Attempt 3 report</span><span style="display:block;font-size:24px;color:#6a655c;margin-top:4px">Submitted 7 Aug 2026</span></span><span style="font-size:24px;color:#6a655c">View</span></div>
</div>
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Divider with label</p>
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:20px"><span style="flex:1;height:2px;background:#efece7"></span><span style="font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">or</span><span style="flex:1;height:2px;background:#efece7"></span></div>
<p style="margin:32px 0 0;font-size:26px;line-height:1.6;color:#6a655c">Use List for generic rows and LessonRow for curriculum, where done, current and not-yet must read at a glance.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p style="margin:24px 0 0;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:25px;font-weight:500;color:#8a847a;border-top:2px solid #e2ded7;padding-top:20px">Table &middot; List &middot; Divider</p>
</section>

<section data-label="Surfaces" data-screen-label="23" data-speaker-notes="Paper versus Card is the distinction people skip, and it causes real mess. A card represents one content object — a course, a result, a lesson. Paper is just a surface: a panel, a well, a sheet. If everything is a Card, then card-specific behaviour like hover-lift starts appearing on things that aren't clickable, and the interface lies about what you can press. Accordion gets the orange-50 open state, which is the same selection idiom as everywhere else." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:76px 100px 56px;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#1a1917;background:#f9f7f4">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Surfaces</h2>
<p style="margin:0 0 52px;font-size:34px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43;max-width:58ch">Card represents one content object. Paper is a surface — a panel, a well, a sheet. Keeping them apart stops hover-lift appearing on things that are not clickable.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Paper tones</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:24px;margin-bottom:44px;flex:0 0 auto">
<div style="background:#fff;border:2px solid #efece7;border-radius:14px;padding:28px;box-shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(26,25,23,.06)"><p style="margin:0 0 8px;font-size:30px;font-weight:600">Default</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:25px;color:#6a655c">elevation 1</p></div>
<div style="background:#f9f7f4;border:2px solid #efece7;border-radius:14px;padding:32px"><p style="margin:0 0 8px;font-size:30px;font-weight:600">Subtle</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:25px;color:#6a655c">section well</p></div>
<div style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fff3ee,#fff8ea);border:2px solid #ffe7dc;border-radius:14px;padding:32px"><p style="margin:0 0 8px;font-size:30px;font-weight:700;color:#8c2f14">Exam in 26 days</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:25px;color:#b23b17">38% through your plan</p></div>
<div style="background:#1a1917;border-radius:14px;padding:32px;box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(26,25,23,.08)"><p style="margin:0 0 8px;font-size:30px;font-weight:600;color:#fff">Inverse</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:25px;color:#cbc6bd">on ink-950</p></div>
</div>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Accordion — one panel open</p>
<div style="border:2px solid #efece7;border-radius:14px;background:#fff;overflow:hidden;flex:0 0 auto">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:20px;padding:28px 32px;background:#fff5f0">
<span style="flex:1;font-size:32px;font-weight:600;color:#b23b17">Domain 1: Design Resilient Architectures</span>
<span style="font-size:26px;color:#6a655c">12 lessons &middot; 26%</span><span style="color:#f0602a;font-size:22px">&#9650;</span></div>
<div style="padding:8px 32px 32px;font-size:28px;line-height:1.6;color:#4e4a43">Multi-AZ patterns, decoupling with SQS and EventBridge, failover and recovery objectives.</div>
</div>
<p style="margin:24px 0 0;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:25px;font-weight:500;color:#8a847a;border-top:2px solid #e2ded7;padding-top:20px">Paper &middot; Accordion &middot; AppBar &middot; Card</p>
</section>

<section data-label="Overlays" data-screen-label="24" data-speaker-notes="Four ways to interrupt, ordered by how much they cost the learner. A snackbar confirms and disappears. A tooltip explains on hover. A dialog demands a decision. A backdrop stops everything. The rule I'd hold to: use the cheapest one that does the job. On a platform where people sit timed exams, a modal that didn't need to be a modal costs someone real seconds — and the submit-attempt dialog is the one case where interrupting is the right call." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:76px 100px 56px;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#1a1917;background:#fff">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Overlays</h2>
<p style="margin:0 0 40px;font-size:33px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43;max-width:66ch">Ordered by cost to the learner: snackbar confirms, tooltip explains, dialog demands a decision, backdrop stops everything. Use the cheapest one that does the job.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.15fr 1fr;gap:56px;flex:1;align-content:start">
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:26px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Dialog</p>
<div style="background:#fff;border-radius:20px;box-shadow:0 24px 56px rgba(26,25,23,.14);overflow:hidden">
<div style="padding:30px 34px 26px">
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:36px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em">Submit attempt?</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:28px;line-height:1.55;color:#4e4a43">14 questions are still unanswered. Submitting ends the attempt and scores it immediately.</p>
</div>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:flex-end;gap:16px;padding:20px 34px;background:#f9f7f4;border-top:2px solid #efece7">
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;height:54px;padding:0 26px;border-radius:10px;border:2px solid #e2ded7;background:#fff;font-size:25px;font-weight:600">Keep going</span>
<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;height:54px;padding:0 26px;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20);color:#fff;font-size:25px;font-weight:600">Submit</span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:28px">
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 18px;font-size:26px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Snackbar</p>
<div style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:18px;padding:18px 24px;background:#12a150;color:#fff;border-radius:10px;box-shadow:0 12px 28px rgba(26,25,23,.1)">
<span style="font-size:26px">&#10003;</span><span style="font-size:28px;font-weight:500">Attempt saved</span>
<span style="font-size:26px;font-weight:600;border:2px solid rgba(255,255,255,.5);padding:8px 18px;border-radius:8px">Undo</span></div>
</div>
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:26px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a847a">Tooltip</p>
<div style="display:inline-flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:12px">
<span style="background:#1a1917;color:#fff;padding:14px 20px;border-radius:8px;font-size:26px;font-weight:500">Flag for review</span>
<span class="wl-ico" data-sz="26" style="width:60px;height:60px;border:2px solid #e2ded7;border-radius:10px;background:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;color:#4e4a43"><i data-lucide="flag"></i></span>
</div>
</div>
<div>
