<p style="margin:0 0 60px;font-size:34px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;color:#4e4a43;max-width:60ch">Lucide at 2px stroke, routed through a single <span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-weight:500">Icon</span> component. Sizes 16 to 24. No emoji, anywhere.</p>
<div id="wl-icons" style="display:flex;gap:52px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#37342e;margin-bottom:56px">
<i data-lucide="play-circle"></i><i data-lucide="clipboard-check"></i><i data-lucide="flask-conical"></i><i data-lucide="award"></i><i data-lucide="trophy"></i><i data-lucide="badge-check"></i><i data-lucide="clock"></i><i data-lucide="calendar"></i><i data-lucide="trending-up"></i><i data-lucide="bookmark"></i><i data-lucide="download"></i><i data-lucide="flag"></i><i data-lucide="bell"></i><i data-lucide="search"></i>
</div>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:30px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.6;color:#6a655c;max-width:70ch;border-top:2px solid #e2ded7;padding-top:36px">This is a documented substitution — no Whizlabs icon set was supplied. Send the real set and it swaps in behind the same component.</p>
</section>

<section data-label="Open items" data-screen-label="29" data-speaker-notes="So where this actually stands. The logo, the three gradient stops and Poppins came from you and are exact — build on those with confidence. The mono, the icons and both screen layouts are my proposals, and I'd rather you correct them now than discover them in production. Send real screens or a Figma file and the UI kits become accurate instead of merely plausible. Everything here is built to be corrected, and that's the point — a system nobody edits is a system nobody uses." style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:space-between;padding:100px;background:#1a1917;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#fff;position:relative;overflow:hidden">
<span style="position:absolute;inset:auto 0 0 0;height:10px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#e8402b,#f0602a 52%,#f78b20)"></span>
<h2 style="margin:0;font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em">Open items</h2>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:56px">
<div style="border-top:2px solid #4e4a43;padding-top:28px"><p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:36px;font-weight:600">The mono</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:28px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.6;color:#aca69c">IBM Plex Mono is a proposal. Confirm it, replace it, or drop it for Poppins.</p></div>
<div style="border-top:2px solid #4e4a43;padding-top:28px"><p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:36px;font-weight:600">The icon set</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:28px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.6;color:#aca69c">Lucide stands in until the real SVG sprite or font arrives.</p></div>
<div style="border-top:2px solid #4e4a43;padding-top:28px"><p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:36px;font-weight:600">The screens</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:28px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.6;color:#aca69c">Both UI kits are reasoned reconstructions. Real screens or Figma make them accurate.</p></div>
</div>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:34px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.5;color:#cbc6bd;max-width:64ch">The logo, the gradient's three stops and Poppins are confirmed and exact. Everything else is a first draft built to be corrected.</p>
</section>

</x-import>

</x-dc>
<script type="text/x-dc" data-dc-script>
class Component extends DCLogic {
  componentDidMount(){ this.hydrateIcons(); }
  componentDidUpdate(){ this.hydrateIcons(); }
  hydrateIcons(){
    const run = () => {
      if (!window.lucide) return;
      // Each host declares its own glyph size, so hydrate host by host.
      const hosts = [
        ...document.querySelectorAll('#wl-icons'),
        ...document.querySelectorAll('.wl-ico')
      ];
      hosts.forEach(h => {
        if (h.dataset.wlHydrated) return;
        const pending = h.querySelectorAll('i[data-lucide]');
        if (!pending.length) return;
        h.dataset.wlHydrated = '1';
        const sz = Number(h.dataset.sz) || 56;
        pending.forEach(i => window.lucide.createIcons({
          nameAttr: 'data-lucide',
          attrs: { width: sz, height: sz, 'stroke-width': 2 },
          icons: undefined,
          root: i.parentElement
        }));
      });
    };
    run();
    if (!window.lucide) window.addEventListener('load', run, { once: true });
    setTimeout(run, 400);
    setTimeout(run, 1200);
  }
}

</script>
</body>
